<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15549" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ē-lumbis</span></b> , e, adj.
		lumbus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>hip-shot</i>, <i>having the hip
				dislocated.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: evulso lumbo, Paul. ex <i><span class="en">Fest.
				p. 76, 13</span></i> Müll. (dub.).
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, of style: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ciceronem male audisse a Bruto, ut ipsius
					verbis utar, tamquam fractum atque elumbem,</span>”
				i. e. <i>enervated</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. Or. 18</span></i>
			.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>: virus, i. e. <i>that
				weakens</i>, <i>enervates</i>, Prud. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στεφ</span>. 2, 216.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
